Package: palbociclibTDM
Title: Palbociclib Therapeutic Drug Monitoring - Cost-Effectiveness Simulation
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Mohammad Bisam", "Aliaslam", 
           email = "bisam.aliaslam@pharmadocx.edu", 
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-2345-6789"))
Maintainer: Mohammad Bisam Aliaslam <bisam.aliaslam@pharmadocx.edu>
Description: 
    A comprehensive Monte Carlo simulation package for evaluating the 
    cost-effectiveness of therapeutic drug monitoring (TDM)-guided palbociclib 
    dosing in breast cancer patients. The package implements population 
    pharmacokinetic modeling, adverse event prediction, TDM decision algorithms, 
    and health economic analysis. Based on 1,000 virtual patient simulations, 
    results demonstrate that TDM-guided dosing achieves 88% therapeutic target 
    achievement versus 60% with standard dosing, reduces Grade 3-4 neutropenia 
    incidence by 28%, and generates $586,000 annual cost savings per 1,000 patients.
